# The Docker build context is the repository root (docker/*.Dockerfile). Nothing that can hold a
# secret, a history or a local install goes in: docker/.env, every .env*, the secrets volume's
# working copies, git, node_modules and build output. .env.example files are kept out too: no image
# needs them, and compose-check.yml fails on any .env file inside an image.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
.claude
**/.env
**/.env.*
docker/.env
docker/secrets
# Only the migrate image needs a file from docker/ (the Dockerfiles themselves are always sent).
docker/*
!docker/ensure-photos-container.cjs
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.log
**/coverage
web/e2e/.output
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
fixtures
evals/**
!evals/package.json
docs
infra
